      "question": "Module 14's `start_attempt` runs inside the engine's run lock (`engine.py:606` is under `_start_task`, which holds the lock), so the lock question is already answered in code. The open part is what to do when the `usage_unreadable` event append fails (PR #141's open question). Today the error propagates and the attempt never starts. Which behaviour do you want?",
