      "header": "Repos step",
      "question": "Appendix A, step 5, says `factory init --github` adds the repo to `repos` in the machine config. The code doesn't: `init --github` only copies the kit, writes `.factory/config/` and creates labels. Nothing reads `repos`, and `factory config init` writes `repos: []` that nothing uses. `tick --all-repos` only finds repos that already have a run, so a new repo is skipped by the scheduler until you start one by hand. Which do you want?",
